# Mechanical CGS units, from NIST SP 811 (2008), appendix B.8, and J. D. Jackson, Classical Electrodynamics,
# 3rd ed., appendix on units. All definitions are exact conversion factors to SI units (F7: no new dimensions).
# Format: symbol:name formula [Type]; '#' starts a comment.

@system CGS
@include si.units
@member cm g s

dyn:dyne 1e-5 N [Force]
erg:erg 1e-7 J [Energy]
Ba:barye 0.1 Pa [Pressure]
Gal:galileo 0.01 m / s^2 [Acceleration]
cm²:square_centimetre cm^2 [Area]
cm³:cubic_centimetre cm^3 [Volume]

# Dynamic and kinematic viscosity have no standard quantity type
P:poise 0.1 Pa s
St:stokes 1e-4 m^2 / s

@prefixed P c m
@prefixed St c
@prefixed Gal m µ

@preferred Length cm
@preferred Mass g
@preferred Force dyn
@preferred Energy erg
@preferred Pressure Ba
@preferred Acceleration Gal
@preferred Area cm²
@preferred Volume cm³
